module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.shared_symbol_projection_is_not_injective

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data shared_symbol_projection_is_not_injective: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "shared_symbol_projection_is_not_injective" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "THE LIVE SPECIMEN THIS ROW CITES IS RESOLVED, 2026-09-26, and by deletion rather than the rename the class witness had declined. Reading `extdeps.git` found `type GitWorktree` had NO CONSUMER in the corpus: declared once, its helper `GitWorktreeHead` read only by that type's own `head` field, and the helper's arms read nowhere. So the collision stood between a faithfully cited upstream service -- `git worktree` is a real git subcommand, so `service git.Worktree` is the DESIGN section 3 citation and stays -- and ten lines of modeling nothing consumed. The unconsumed side is deleted, which removes the collision at its root and discharges a section 3c dangling declaration in the same motion; a rename would have preserved dead modeling under a new name. THE CLASS IS NOT DISCHARGED BY THIS: the projection `sanitize_service_name` remains many-to-one by declaration, the emitter wall remains its repair, and the discriminating RED remains the isolated fixture in test.claim.emitted_symbol_collision_witness_test, which never sourced its red from this module and so lost nothing when the specimen went.",

    "HOW THE SPECIMEN SURVIVED, WHICH IS THE PART WORTH KEEPING. It was an EMIT-TIME blocking error, and no required lane emits that closure: a required witnesses floor run over the same head evaluated 531 claims and passed while `gunbc compile --entry dag/extdeps/git/git.dag` refused with one blocking error. That is DESIGN section 3's note about the population a run compiles, observed rather than predicted -- outside the required gate the substrate still refuses and nothing asks it to. The gap is not this row's subject and is recorded here because this specimen is the evidence for it.",


    "shared symbol projection is not injective (A NAME-TO-SYMBOL PROJECTION SHARED BY EVERY TARGET ERASES A DISTINCTION THE SOURCE CARRIED. Until the emit fold, nothing refused, so two distinct identities silently became one emitted symbol. Emit now refuses EmittedSymbolCollision; the invalid source state remains writable.",

    "THE INVALID STATE is two distinct authored identities that project to one emitted symbol. Before the wall the second definition overwrote or shadowed the first and rustc, not the compiler, was the first observer (E0428). Silent emit of a colliding pair is outside the ladder (DESIGN.md section 5).",

    "RECEIPT, observed rather than argued: `sanitize_service_name` splits the authored name on '.' and joins the capitalized segments with nothing, so the segment boundary is erased. Two services named `collision.Probe` and `CollisionProbe` in one module emitted two `pub struct CollisionProbe` definitions and bound one parameter for both, with zero blocking diagnostics. `service_var_name` is the second channel, since to_snake of one symbol is one symbol.",

    "LIVE SPECIMEN, gunbc#11518 / session vivid-wolf-601: `extdeps.git` declares `type GitWorktree` and `service git.Worktree` in one module. They are two identities. Emit wrote both as `pub struct GitWorktree` in `extdeps_git.rs` and rustc reported E0428. DuplicateDeclaration did not fire because the authored names differ. That is this class, not a collector that admitted one declaration twice.",

    "THE WALL NOW LANDS at emit: `emitted_symbol_collision_diagnostics` folds each module's type declarations and sanitized service names onto one emitted symbol and refuses `EmittedSymbolCollision`, blocking, the same shape as `module_filename_collision_diagnostics`. Executing evidence: `test.claim.emitted_symbol_collision_witness`. The invalid state remains writable in source, so this is rung 2, not construction.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mechanically preventable on the emit path. The sibling projection at the same grain, `module_to_filename`, was already at that grain: it maps '.' to '_' and is equally many-to-one, but `module_filename_collision_diagnostics` refuses on the collision and all three emitters call it. This row's service-name instance now has the same wall.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: when a projection from authored names to emitted symbols DELETES a separator rather than escaping it, it is many-to-one, and the question is not whether a collision is likely but whether anything observes one. Grep the projection's call sites: if every one of them consumes the result directly and none of them folds the whole population first, there is no observer and the collision is silent.",

    "ATTAINABLE CEILING: structurally impossible once an emitted-symbol allocation cannot share a symbol across distinct authored identities. Until then the wall is rung 2: decidable refusal, state still writable.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMED AS A CAPABILITY AND NOT AS A RENAME: `sanitize_service_name` (and `service_var_name`) becomes injective against the type-declaration namespace — service symbols carry a distinguishing element a type name cannot produce — ANSWERING BY EXECUTION over `type GitWorktree` beside `service git.Worktree` in one emitted module with no EmittedSymbolCollision. A rename of this one pair satisfies a rename while every future collision still lands. Adding the diagnostic variant is no longer the missing capability.",

    "WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED: renaming the live `extdeps.git` declarations. The emitter must refuse the collision; the source names remain two facts.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.emit_core_support", decl_name: "emitted_symbol_collision_diagnostics", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.emit_core_support", decl_name: "sanitize_service_name", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
